      <figcaption>
        Kloster Indersdorf, Bavaria. The twelfth-century monastery ran as an UNRRA children&rsquo;s centre after the war, taking in unaccompanied children and teenagers who had come out of the camps and the hiding places. Helen was one of them in 1946.
        <span class="cite">Photograph by H. Helmlechner &middot; CC BY-SA 4.0 via Wikimedia Commons</span>
      </figcaption>
