    <div class="panel">
      <span class="lbl">Why this place is on the map</span>
      <p>The children&rsquo;s centre is where the postwar half of Helen&rsquo;s route becomes documented again. She appears in the Indersdorf records, then at Prien am Chiemsee, then on a sponsorship file, then on a passenger list. Five places, four archives, one girl.</p>
      <p>It is also where the only photograph we have of her from those years was taken, standing with her friend Ibi Weinberger.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="sources">Everything else on this site concerns Helen&rsquo;s own family: the Helmans, the Land&oacute;s and the Sperbers. The map is the one place where her husband&rsquo;s family appears alongside them. The photograph of Kloster Indersdorf is by H. Helmlechner, used under CC BY-SA 4.0; every other image on this site is a family document or a family photograph.</p>

  <p class="maplabel"><span class="tag">Interactive</span> Click any pin for the record behind it. Drag to move, scroll to zoom, open the timeline index, and switch on a single person&rsquo;s path.</p>
